    "event": {
      "address": "Graces Alley, London E1 8JB",
      "all_day": false,
      "category": "music",
      "dedupe_key": "mikado|2027-03-16|wiltons-music",
      "description": "Charles Court Opera ‘s highly successful production of The Mikado returns to bring ‘five-star heaven’ (WhatsOnStage) to Wilton’s Music Hall. Following their critically acclaimed productions of Iolanthe and Patience, the “masters of G&S” present their stylish production of one of the most loved of Gilbert and Sullivan ’s comic masterpieces. Behind closed doors at a British Consulate, the scheming Lord High Executioner is about to hatch one plot too far, with far-reaching and hilarious consequences for everyone involved. Containing familiar songs including “A wandering minstrel, I”, “I’ve got a little list” and “Three little maids from school”, this punchy and hilarious satire promises to be a treat for operetta lovers and newcomers alike. Directed by CCO’s Artistic Director, John Savournin, and featuring a first class cast including Matthew Kellett, Catrine Kirkman, Meriel Cunningham, Robin Bailey, Llio Evans, Fiona Finsbury and Matthew Palmer, this is one production you definitely do not want to miss! ★★★★★ “five-star heaven” – WhatsOnStage ★★★★ “This is a triumphant achievement both visually and musically” – The Stage ★★★★★ “This production simply cannot be bettered” – The Spy in the Stalls",
      "ends_at": "2027-03-20T21:20:00Z",
